Upstream 8cc8bcbf6b (#41141, MCP Events webhooks) builds the webhook client
with NodeHttpClient.layerUndiciOptions from the @effect/platform-node barrel.
That keeps @effect/platform-node's Undici module in the CLI bundle, whose
`export * from "undici"` becomes a static ESM import of the external undici
package. `cli.ts build-exe` refuses it ("imports file-backed packages that a
single-executable cannot resolve: undici"), so the Linux x64 runtime does not
build on upstream main from #41141 on (stack build 45127747387).

The client now comes from NodeHttpClient.layerNodeHttpOptions({ lookup }),
imported from @effect/platform-node/NodeHttpClient like the other server
clients. The same DNS lookup refuses names that resolve to a private address
when the socket connects, and redirects still come back unfollowed
(McpWebhookTransport.test.ts covers both). The bundle holds no static undici
import afterwards.

Drop this commit once upstream builds its single-executable from main again.

